		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: What's the best way to pin a rigid body to another rigid body?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=42437#p42437"><![CDATA[
The best way is to create a new URDF and attach them as a fixed joint. You can use the URDF editor to do this.<br><br>See this example how to combine a car and a kuka:<br><a href="https://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3/blob/master/examples/pybullet/gym/pybullet_utils/examples/combineUrdf.py" class="postlink">https://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet ... ineUrdf.py</a><br><br>Alternatively, you get some loose coupling (not stiff) using addUserConstraint, which is not recommended in general.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Thu Oct 24, 2019 1:58 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
